<title>USA: Nokia eases in New York.</title>
<headline>Nokia eases in New York.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish mobile phone maker Nokia Group's stock price eased on Friday in New York, weighed by profit-taking after the company reported results.</p>
<p>The company's American Depositary Receipts fell 1-3/4 to 62-1/4. Volume by late afternoon was 1.2 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;There's some profit-taking,&quot; a trader said. &quot;They were down a bit yesterday and it's just follow-through&quot; from Thursday's 3-1/8 point drop.</p>
<p>Nokia reported earnings on Thursday that were in line with market expectations. However, it raised its dividend and said it expected strong growth and profitability to continue in 1997.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
